  "poseDistinctnessContract": "Export FAILS if any two poses of one species hash the same OR are closer than 3% of that species wingspan by symmetric Hausdorff distance. The crowd system in this project shipped a naive sine gait that made two poses byte-identical and nothing caught it; a flock doing that stutters across the whole sky.",
  "objConvention": "Unreal legacy OBJ adapter: canonical vertices are centimetres in the bird frame (+X forward, +Y right, +Z up, origin at the body centre); this file is written with Y reflected and triangle winding reversed. One object, exactly two g groups (plumage_main, plumage_hood), so the importer creates exactly two material slots.",
  "materialSlotContract": "Exactly two g groups per mesh -> exactly two material slots: plumage_main then plumage_hood. This module applies no material; plumage colours below are recorded intent.",
